1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
The mountains on China's 20-yuan note are a real place.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,300
I'm your China Travel Expert.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,000
It's the Li River near Xingping, in Guilin.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,800
Karst peaks curve around the water — chosen for the note in 1999.

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,600
Stand at the exact viewpoint for just 20 yuan.

6
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,200
That's about three US dollars.

7
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,600
A bamboo raft past the peaks runs around 216 yuan.

8
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,900
Double-tap if you'd frame this shot.

9
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,100
★ Expert Tip: Hike free Laozhai Hill for the same view, fewer crowds.

10
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,800
Cruise boat — or bamboo raft?
